    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8761",
      "problem": "Sketch the graph of $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y = -\\dfrac{1}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\dfrac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244490/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\dfrac 1 5$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{5x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244490/assets/30ace3126ec127b9949ebf599d615020b9770458825d22460e9e7e0b3d5efec3.png)",
